From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aditya kale <252700881+kaleaditya28897-linux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:38:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] hurd: gai_misc.h: static inline helpers (clang inlines
 differently)

__gai_start_notify_thread and __gai_create_helper_thread were extern
inline (GNU89): no copy of their own, so a call the compiler doesn't
inline is an undefined symbol.  GCC inlines them; clang left one call in
libanl.  Nothing changes for GCC.  Joist, Phase 5 step 7.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sysdeps/mach/hurd/gai_misc.h | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sysdeps/mach/hurd/gai_misc.h b/sysdeps/mach/hurd/gai_misc.h
index 20f15135..16cc818e 100644
--- a/sysdeps/mach/hurd/gai_misc.h
+++ b/sysdeps/mach/hurd/gai_misc.h
@@ -22,7 +22,9 @@
 #define gai_start_notify_thread __gai_start_notify_thread
 #define gai_create_helper_thread __gai_create_helper_thread
 
-extern inline void
+/* static inline, not extern inline: an extern inline (GNU89) function has
+   no copy of its own, and only GCC inlines every call of these.  */
+static inline void
 __gai_start_notify_thread (void)
 {
   sigset_t ss;
@@ -32,7 +34,7 @@ __gai_start_notify_thread (void)
   assert_perror (sigerr);
 }
 
-extern inline int
+static inline int
 __gai_create_helper_thread (pthread_t *threadp, void *(*tf) (void *),
 			    void *arg)
 {
